# UNLOCK — Coding Standards

- Prefer clear TypeScript and explicit domain/application types.
- Keep functions/modules focused and names aligned with the domain glossary.
- Preserve existing conventions unless there is a concrete reason to change them.
- Avoid speculative abstractions and unrelated refactors.
- Handle expected errors deliberately; do not swallow unexpected failures.
- Keep tests behavior-focused and deterministic where possible.
- Comments should explain non-obvious intent, not restate the code.
- Keep diffs small enough to review confidently.
